  "instruction": "Give me a list of all of the fish that Albacore form mixed schools with, but ignore the ones that can live over 20 years.",
  "answer": "Based on the research from authoritative sources (FishBase, NOAA Fisheries, Animal Diversity Web citing FAO Species Catalogue), the fish species documented to form mixed schools with Albacore tuna (*Thunnus alalunga*) with maximum lifespan ≤ 20 years are:\n\n| Species | Scientific Name | Max Lifespan | Source |\n|---------|-----------------|--------------|--------|\n| Skipjack tuna | *Katsuwonus pelamis* | 12 years | FishBase / NOAA |\n| Yellowfin tuna | *Thunnus albacares* | 18 years | FishBase / NOAA |\n| Southern bluefin tuna | *Thunnus maccoyii* | 20 years | FishBase |\n| Pacific bluefin tuna | *Thunnus orientalis* | 15 years | FishBase |\n\n**Excluded (lifespan > 20 years):**\n- Atlantic bluefin tuna (*Thunnus thynnus*) — documented to school with Albacore but max lifespan ~40 years\n\n**Not verified as mixed-school associates:** Bigeye tuna, Pacific saury, anchovies — these appear in lifespan databases but lack explicit citations confirming mixed schooling with Albacore in the authoritative sources checked.\n\n## Sources\n- FishBase *Thunnus alalunga* summary (Ref. 168: Collette & Nauen 1983): https://fishbase.se/summary/Speciessummary.php?id=142\n- NOAA Fisheries North Atlantic Albacore Tuna: https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/north-atlantic-albacore-tuna\n- NOAA Fisheries Pacific Albacore Tuna: https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/pacific-albacore-tuna\n- Animal Diversity Web *Thunnus alalunga*: https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Thunnus_alalunga\n- FishBase *Katsuwonus pelamis*: https://www.fishbase.se/summary/107\n- FishBase *Thunnus albacares*: https://www.fishbase.se/summary/thunnus-albacares\n- FishBase *Thunnus maccoyii*: https://www.fishbase.se/summary/Speciessummary.php?id=145\n- FishBase *Thunnus orientalis*: https://fishbase.se/summary/Speciessummary.php?id=14290",
